<title>Dementia with Lewy Bodies: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0428-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Suspected cognitive dysfunction. Evaluate activities of daily living (ADL) and mental status (MS).</label>
<path target="cell-7">Normal ADL, impaired MS</path>
<path target="cell-8">Abnormal ADL, normal MS</path>
<path target="cell-9">Abnormal ADL, impaired MS</path>
<path target="cell-10">Normal ADL, normal MS</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Mild cognitive impairment.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Consider depression or frontotemporal dementia.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Dementia.</label>
<path target="cell-11"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-11">
<label>Evaluate for treatable causes with laboratory testing and neuroimaging.</label>
<path target="cell-12">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-13">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>Treat subdural hematoma, brain tumor, normal pressure hydrocephalus, metabolic encephalopathies, others.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-13">
<label>Temporal link to stroke?</label>
<path target="cell-15">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-14">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-14">
<label>Recent parkinsonism, prominent hallucinations, delirium (fluctuating cognition)?</label>
<path target="cell-16">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-17">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-16">
<label>Dementia with Lewy bodies.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-17">
<label>Alzheimer's disease, frontotemporal dementia, or primary progressive aphasia.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-15">
<label>Dementia with cerebrovascular disease.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>Cognitively intact.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>From Knopma DS, Boeve BF, Peterson RC. Essentials of the proper diagnoses of mild cognitive impairment, pementia, and major subtypes of dementia. <em>Mayo Clin Proc</em> 2003;<strong>78</strong>:1290&#x2013;1308.<xref ref="pubmed14531488" resource="acc002" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
